{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact clean pushed head 7c535c63c6319ef8953b9836fefbca4c1995dd47, over both artifacts: docs 674f030b and cmd/gs 6dbed803.\n\nPath coverage is now correct and that part is settled. The cumulative diff against main is eighteen files: four under cmd/gs and exactly fourteen documentation pages, which I counted from the diff rather than from your description, and the two artifacts cover all of it. The complaint codex raised at e63a210f against my earlier verdict does not apply to this one.\n\nThree reasons to change, in the order I would fix them.\n\nONE, and this is the finding. The change stated purpose is not pinned by any test. I reverted the six durable-write commands to ignore the advertisement entirely -- stateCommand main.go:317, reviewCommandWithValidator :395, mergeCommand :457, ratifyCommand :1187, supersedeCommand :1223, batchCommand :1341, each rewritten to use *serverFlag directly -- and go build exits 0 and the whole cmd/gs suite passes in 111 seconds. I ran that myself rather than relaying it. Not one assertion fails. The same holds for the four query commands at :1757, :1811, :1953 and :2007. So of the eleven commands this head rewires, only statusCommand and askResident are actually pinned; the other ten could be reverted to main behaviour and every gate would stay green.\n\nThat matters more than usual here because 291 new lines of test read as though they cover this. They do not measure it. A reader seeing resident_default_test.go would reasonably conclude the default is protected, and it is not.\n\nWhat would fix it: one test per family that proves the advertisement is used with no flag. A durable write against a published counting resident, asserting the request counter moved and the event landed in the resident log; and one query the same way. TestPublishedResidentAnswersWithoutServerFlag already shows the right instrument -- count requests, do not compare output shape -- so this is extending a pattern you have, not inventing one.\n\nTWO. main_test.go loses TestValidateLoopbackServer, and with it the only thing in cmd/gs pinning that an explicit malformed or non-loopback --server is refused rather than degraded. Making resolveServerURL return an explicit flag unvalidated at :1631 also leaves the suite green. residentclient re-validates so no socket opens, but the behaviour silently changes from refuse to fall back locally, which is the exact fail-open the deleted openForQuery comment existed to prevent. Restore that coverage somewhere in cmd/gs.\n\nTHREE. The exact head is red. go test ./internal/docset/ -run TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord fails at 7c535c63 and passes at main; I ran both. The head is behind main, and main 70f4ab0a re-anchored the nexus-to-host artifact move, so nine pages here still name the retired 94cadf30 -- two of them pages this head edits. This is not an authoring error and I am not asking you to hand-edit rests_on: re-anchoring is a merge-coordinator step and the implementing commits on this branch correctly do not touch front matter. It does mean the head cannot merge as it stands and needs a carry onto current main. Since that changes the head anyway, folding one and two into the same carry costs nothing.\n\nArchitecture: layers 3 and 7. This changes the default flag behaviour of eleven gs subcommands, which is the surface compatibility axis, and it changes the client-behaviour half of the advertisement contract. The head does update docs/reference/architecture.md:212-216 and the edit is substantive rather than cosmetic -- reads fall back locally while naming the refusal, durable writes refuse rather than folding locally -- and I checked both halves against the code. docs/reference/gs/serve.md:106-117 names two real limits honestly, including that the CLI and cmd/gitseq-mcp knowingly disagree on a non-loopback advertisement, which I confirmed at cmd/gitseq-mcp/main.go:162-169. One gap: the cmd/gs bullet at :687-698 still describes the CLI with no mention of default routing, so the same surface is now described at two fidelities.\n\nSecurity: no new authority. The URL comes from .git/gitseq/resident.json via ResidentURL (internal/app/resident.go:60-66), the record genesis must equal this checkout, and ValidateURL requires an http loopback host with no credentials, path, query or fragment. A non-loopback advertisement is refused before any dial and that is pinned. No environment variable influences it. The boundary does widen in practice: any local process that can write the common .git now redirects every read and write for every user of the repo with no flag typed, and reads are checked only by genesis and head-string equality, never by verifying the projection body. I am not treating that as blocking, because architecture.md:229-231 already declares this is not a defence against a hostile local process. But the unchanged sentence at :211, that the advertisement confers nothing, reads weaker than it did before this change, and the head does not qualify it. Worth a sentence in the carry.\n\nSimplification: the query.go deletion is a genuine improvement -- openForQuery second validation entry point is gone and its behaviour is preserved at main.go:1630-1632, so nothing functional was lost. Nothing here is fluff. The - sentinel is a good escape hatch, though the flag help string at eleven sites still says only \"resident sequencer URL\" and mentions neither the sentinel nor the advertised default, which contradicts docs/reference/gs/state.md. Non-blocking, worth folding into the carry.\n\nI want to name what the tests do well, because the gap above is not carelessness. TestAdvertisedResidentWithDivergentFrontierIsRefused and TestAskResidentRefusesDivergentWorkQueryFrontier each serve the resident own real answer with exactly one field lied about, so only the guard under test can refuse it. That is the right shape and their fails-by-name comments are true. The weak one is TestAdvertisedNonLoopbackURLIsRefused, which asserts only that the error is non-nil, so it does not pin that the message names loopback or offers the --server - way out.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:674f030b72be10f659b6e47436be027b58c3b7a4","head":"7c535c63c6319ef8953b9836fefbca4c1995dd47","verdict":"changes-requested"}}